      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Render wide Markdown tables without breaking message layout",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- render Markdown tables inside a dedicated horizontal-scroll wrapper\n- preserve native table layout and column sizing\n- keep wide tables contained within the message surface on narrow screens\n- regenerate the checked-in embedded webassets\n\n## Why\n\nWide Markdown tables could overflow the message layout. Applying scrolling directly to the table also changes it from native table layout, which can break grid sizing. The wrapper provides overflow containment while the table remains `display: table`.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nVerified in a real Chromium browser at a 480 x 720 viewport using the production table renderer and styles.\n\n| Observation | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Scroll wrapper width | `clientWidth = 402px` |\n| Wide content width | `scrollWidth = 1034px` |\n| Wrapper overflow | `overflow-x: auto` |\n| Table layout | `display: table` |\n| Rendered table width | `1034.234px` |\n| Horizontal interaction | `scrollLeft: 0 -> 260` |\n| GFM column alignment | left / center / right preserved |\n| Console | 0 warnings, 0 errors |\n\nBefore horizontal scroll:\n\n![Wide Markdown table contained at a narrow viewport](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jjjhenriksen/clickclack/codex/markdown-tables-pr/docs/review-proof/markdown-table-narrow.png)\n\nAfter horizontal scroll:\n\n![Wide Markdown table scrolled horizontally while the message remains contained](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jjjhenriksen/clickclack/codex/markdown-tables-pr/docs/review-proof/markdown-table-scrolled.png)\n\nAlignment regression check:\n\n![GFM left, center, and right column alignment preserved](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jjjhenriksen/clickclack/codex/markdown-tables-pr/docs/review-proof/markdown-table-alignment.png)\n\n## Validation\n\n- `pnpm check`\n- `pnpm build`\n- repeatability gate: `git diff --exit-code -- apps/api/internal/webassets/dist`\n- Autoreview: clean, no actionable findings\n- ClawSweeper final pass: no findings, security cleared, real-behavior proof sufficient, `patch is correct` (0.95)\n",
